      "rationale": "Re-read the actual pending-row -> readIngressMessage -> acceptsLegacySource -> shouldForward -> matchesAllRegexPatterns -> parseRegex chain. Database input is JSON-decoded and message identity/text fields are checked before filtering; invalid classification remains needs_review. Configured regular expressions are intentional filter input, not HTML/code execution. The new helper extraction preserves nested-quantifier rejection, the 150-character compiled-pattern cap, removal of stateful g/y flags and 100-entry cache. Every production match in this flow truncates text to 8000 characters and calls safeRegexTest with a 100-ms VM CPU timeout; VM exceptions reject the filter. This bound is not inferred solely from the heuristic: the actual vm.runInContext call still executes regex.test with timeout, and the existing test exercised a matching-engine timeout and verified its native timeout cause during this review. The reported source-to-RegExp construction trace omits the bounded match boundary. No unlimited match execution was found in this reported flow. Independently re-read complete e58bd77 filters/ingress delta and persisted ingress caller. Plain string content.text is now permitted solely for messageCustomServiceAction, not messageText; caption validation remains formatted-only. MESSAGE_TYPES does not map this service action, so getMessageTextAndType returns empty text and the service type. The helper also explicitly returns empty text for a primitive string instead of consuming it as ordinary signal text. Normal formatted text is unchanged. Regex compile cap, heuristic, flag/cache logic, 8000-character truncation and actual 100-ms VM timeout remain byte-identical. New persisted-restart and ordinary-message rejection tests independently passed. No additional unbounded matching path is introduced by admitting the non-text service envelope.",
